      ":question/problem": "A survey conducted among $100$ families found that $32$ of them have a dog, $43$ of them have a cat, and $5$ families have both dogs and cats. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a family is randomly selected among the $100$ families, what is the probability that it has at least one of these pets?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
